From 5072fc57ab9fe5338e5ce3af7473bc57d32bb6f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:49:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prose profile: a gigabyte of disk

650 MiB left about 450 free, and BFS cannot be grown afterwards: Haiku's
own disk system add-on has B_DISK_SYSTEM_SUPPORTS_RESIZING commented out,
so DriveSetup cannot offer it and the size chosen at build time is the
size it stays.

Room is nearly free to ship. The unused space is zeros, so an image
compresses to under a third in the installer -- 686 MiB became 196 -- and
a larger one adds almost nothing to a download.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0056-prose-profile-a-gigabyte-of-disk.patch 5edd02754e01154d34ea579709eaf4ec1ce76741a021954429fd88df78a92e09
---
 build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
index f2a5e5d2cc..a15813595b 100644
--- a/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
+++ b/build/jam/DefaultBuildProfiles
@@ -198,9 +198,15 @@ rule DefineDefaultBuildProfiles
 			HAIKU_IMAGE_LABEL ?= Prose ;
 			HAIKU_MMC_LABEL ?= Prose ;
 			if $(DEBUG) != 0 {
-				HAIKU_IMAGE_SIZE ?= 850 ;
+				HAIKU_IMAGE_SIZE ?= 1400 ;
 			}
-			HAIKU_IMAGE_SIZE ?= 650 ;
+			# A gigabyte, of which the system uses about 200 MiB. Room costs
+			# almost nothing to ship: the free space is zeros, and an image
+			# compresses to under a third of its size in the installer.
+			# BFS cannot be grown afterwards -- Haiku's own disk system add-on
+			# has B_DISK_SYSTEM_SUPPORTS_RESIZING commented out -- so the size
+			# chosen here is the size it stays.
+			HAIKU_IMAGE_SIZE ?= 1024 ;
 
 			# The regular image's packages that exist for arm64 -- built by
 			# HaikuArmQemu's prosepkg, the package server has none of them --
